  "_comment": "Hand-written input for characterize_pdk.py. Everything PDK-specific lives here; the script is generic. Netlist parameters (W, L, nf) are the device line values; 'map' turns them into PCell parameters. Output: pdk.json next to this file.",
  "_comment_format": "Generated by pdk_convert.py from convert.json. Compact tree (WorkDir/pdk/pdk_tree.py, .claude/knowledge/pdk_files.md): \"@name\" = value from @refs; a dict with @members is a family that expands to one entry per member, {var} = the member's value, @when = per-member conditions, key+ appends to a list.",
  "_comment_merge_layers": "Implant/marker layers the structure placer may fill as one rectangle over neighbouring devices of the same model in one row, never across rows (npc across rows breaks licon.13; 05_miller_ota draws nsdm per row by hand). nsdm 93/44, psdm 94/20, npc 95/20, lvtn 125/44, urpm 79/20.",
  "_comment_fill": "A ring fill (n-well) encloses the ring's tap_layer by the DRC-measured enclosure; it is never allowed to shrink inside the tap (DRC alone accepts an n+ tap outside the n-well). tap_band = tap width as a function of GRW.",
  "_comment_pcell_patch": "pdk.json is characterised with a patched PCell (2026-11-06, by hand in the container, root, backup .orig next to it): libs.tech/klayout/python/cells/via_generator.py:124 npc_enc 0.01 -> 0.02, so npc encloses every poly licon by 0.10 (licon.15; was 0.09). Re-apply after a new container, then re-run this characterisation.",
  "pdk": "sky130A",
  "container": {
    "name": "iic-osic-tools_xvnc_uid_501",
    "pcell_macro": "$PDK_ROOT/$PDK/libs.tech/klayout/pymacros/sky130_pcells.lym",
    "drc": [
      {
        "tool": "klayout",
        "deck": "$PDK_ROOT/$PDK/libs.tech/klayout/drc/sky130A_mr.drc",
        "vars": {"feol": "true", "beol": "true", "offgrid": "true"}
      },
      {
        "tool": "klayout",
        "deck": "$PDK_ROOT/$PDK/libs.tech/klayout/drc/sky130A_feol_on.lydrc",
        "vars": {},
        "_comment": "Full old deck (licon.7/12/15, difftap.8-11, poly.9, capm.11). Not shipped: a copy of sky130A.lydrc with FEOL = true and source($input, $top_cell), made by hand in the container (2026-11-06, same as designs/klayout/pymacros/full_drc.py). Re-create after a new container."
      },
      {
        "tool": "magic",
        "rcfile": "$PDK_ROOT/$PDK/libs.tech/magic/sky130A.magicrc",
        "style": "drc(full)",
        "_comment": "The KLayout deck has only difftap.1-3: no n-well enclosure/spacing of diff and tap (difftap.8-11), no capm.11. magic's tech file has the full rule set."
      }
    ]
  },
  "_comment_drc_ignore": "Rules evaluated over the whole layout, not per fixture, ignored in every scan: vpp.5a/b/c = max met3/met4/met5 density inside vpp, computed against the total vpp area of the GDS (sky130A.lydrc lines 406-408), so they fire with any other vpp fixture in the same file (2026-11-10).",
  "drc_ignore": ["klayout:vpp.5a", "klayout:vpp.5b", "klayout:vpp.5c"],
  "_comment_structure_gap_range": "Scan range of structure-to-structure gaps (um): above the largest spacing between structures, deep n-well (photodiode): dnwell.3 6.3, dnwell to nwell 4.5.",
  "structure_gap_range": [0.0, 8.0],
  "library": "skywater130",
  "technology": null,
  "dbu": 0.001,
  "grid": 0.005,
  "netlist_defaults": {"nf": 1},
  "netlist_copies": ["m", "mult", "mf", "vm"],
  "_comment_snap": "snap_params: PCell parameter -> grid it is rounded to before drawing. The res_poly PCell draws len on 0.01 um (len 2.877 gives a 3.000 um body), FETs and the MIM cap on the 5 nm manufacturing grid.",
  "_comment_netlist": "netlist_copies: instance keywords that give the number of parallel copies, first one present wins (xschem writes both m= and mult=; the MIM cap uses MF=, the varactor VM=). terms are in PCell parameters (after map and snap_params to the grid).",
  "guard_rings": {
    "rings": {
      "@members": {
        "p_ring": {
          "implant": "psdm",
          "for": ["nmos", "res"],
          "fill": [],
          "@set": {
            "_comment": "p+ tap ring tied to VSS. sky130 has no p-well drawing layer, so nothing to fill. With con_lev=metal1 the PCell draws grw >= 0.23 whatever is asked, hence grw_nominal 0.23."
          }
        },
        "n_ring": {
          "implant": "nsdm",
          "for": ["pmos"],
          "fill": [{"name": "nwell", "layer": "@nwell"}],
          "@set": {
            "_comment": "n+ tap ring tied to VDD; one n-well covers the ring and everything inside it."
          }
        }
      },
      "pcell": "guard_ring_gen",
      "fixed": {"implant_type": "{implant}", "con_lev": "metal1"},
      "map": {"in_w": "IW", "in_l": "IL", "grw": "GRW"},
      "opening": {"x0": "0", "y0": "0"},
      "tap_layer": "@tap",
      "tap_band": "GRW",
      "for_class": "{for}",
      "fill": "{fill}",
      "grw_nominal": 0.23,
      "sweep": {"IW": [3.0, 5.0, 8.0], "IL": [3.0, 6.0], "GRW": [0.23, 0.3, 0.5]},
      "terms": ["1", "IW", "IL", "GRW"]
    }
  },
  "_comment_pins": "Pin shapes per device class (the PCells carry no pin labels); a device's own \"pins\" replaces its class's. Each group: merged shapes on `layer`, minus `minus` if given, optionally only those interacting / not interacting another layer, sorted along `order`; `count` shapes expected. Every rect edge is fitted linearly in `terms` over the device sweep, with k = shape index, first/last = 1 on the end shapes; centres must fit exactly. A size that is not linear (S/D strip length steps with the contact count, w - len in 0.07..0.42; width 0.29 instead of 0.23 on short strips) is stored as a lower bound over the sweep plus the dense bound_sweep (slopes fitted to all samples, constant lowered to the worst one) and <size>_min = smallest sample; size = max of both, so the pin rect lies inside the real metal. size_terms: own terms per size. Gate pad width grows with l: bound over a dense L sweep. MOS: sd = met1 S/D columns (k = 0..nf, none connected; even/odd columns are the two terminals, which one is source is the router's choice), gate = met1 gate pads, one per finger, not connected. res: n1/n2 met1 end pads (k = 0 bottom). cap: met4 top plate over capm, met4 bottom-plate strap. Groups named after a terminal are that terminal's pins (viewer / 012 detail); ring = the shape is a closed ring: the rect is its outer bbox, ring_w its narrowest band. centre_tol (um): centres may miss the linear fit by this much (diodes: the PCell rounds the off-grid w / l of the area-perim sweep, met1 centre off by up to 3 nm; viewer pins only, not routed). Terminal order from the PDK's extraction (magic sky130A.tech device lines, KLayout LVS deck): var c0 = gate (met1 pads on the poly ends), c1 = n-well taps (met1 strips), b = substrate (nothing drawn); diodes: first terminal n = the diffusion (met1), second p = the well tap ring (li1); photodiode d0 = P (outer p-tap ring, li1), d1 = N (the small n-tap in the centre). var / diodes / bjt / photodiode / vpp are placed but not routed inside the block.",
  "pins": {
    "nmos": "@mos_pins",
    "pmos": "@mos_pins",
    "res": {"ends": {"layer": "@met1", "order": "y", "count": "2", "terms": ["1", "len", "k", "k*len"]}},
    "cap": {
      "top": {"layer": "@met4", "interacting": "@capm", "order": "x", "count": "1", "terms": ["1", "w", "l"]},
      "bottom": {
        "layer": "@met4",
        "not_interacting": "@capm",
        "order": "x",
        "count": "1",
        "terms": ["1", "w", "l"]
      }
    },
    "var": {
      "c0": {
        "layer": "@met1",
        "interacting": "@poly",
        "order": "y",
        "count": "2",
        "terms": ["1", "w", "l", "k", "k*w", "k*l"]
      },
      "c1": {
        "layer": "@met1",
        "interacting": "@tap",
        "order": "x",
        "count": "2",
        "terms": ["1", "w", "l", "k", "k*w", "k*l"]
      }
    },
    "ndiode": "@diode_pins",
    "pdiode": "@diode_pins",
    "photodiode": {
      "d0": {"layer": "@li1", "interacting": "@psdm", "order": "x"},
      "d1": {"layer": "@li1", "interacting": "@areaid.photo", "order": "x"}
    }
  },
  "_comment_pin_labels": "Fixed cells (BJTs, VPP) without a pins group: a terminal's pin = the shape under its text label. Layers [drawing, pin, label] searched in this order (a terminal labelled on two layers takes the first); per label the pin-purpose shape under it, else the drawn one. Label = terminal name (any case) or its alias, else a label starting with the terminal name (npn s = SUBSTRATE, c = C). vpp: b = SUB, m3/m4/m5 = MET3/MET4/MET5.",
  "pin_labels": {
    "layers": [
      ["@met5", "@met5.pin", "@met5.label"],
      ["@met4", "@met4.pin", "@met4.label"],
      ["@met3", "@met3.pin", "@met3.label"],
      ["@met2", "@met2.pin", "@met2.label"],
      ["@met1", "@met1.pin", "@met1.label"],
      ["@li1", "@li1.pin", "@li1.label"],
      ["@pwell", "@pwell.pin", "@pwell.label"]
    ],
    "alias": {"b": "SUB", "m3": "MET3", "m4": "MET4", "m5": "MET5"}
  },
  "_comment_routing_rules": "In-block routing (lib/block_router), copied into pdk.json as is: SkyWater periphery rules m1.1/m1.2, m2.1/m2.2, m3.1/m3.2, m4.1/m4.2, m5.1/m5.2 (width/space; met4/met5 only for MIM cap pins), via.1a/via.4a/via.5a, m2.4/m2.5 (via1 cut and met1/met2 enclosure on two / the other two sides), via2.1a/via2.4/via2.5, m3.4. pin / label: the purpose layers export_gds writes block pins and net names on.",
  "routing": {
    "layers": {
      "metals": {
        "@members": {
          "met1": {"n": 68, "w": 0.14},
          "met2": {"n": 69, "w": 0.14},
          "met3": {"n": 70, "w": 0.3},
          "met4": {"n": 71, "w": 0.3},
          "met5": {"n": 72, "w": 1.6}
        },
        "gds": ["{n}", 20],
        "pin": ["{n}", 16],
        "label": ["{n}", 5],
        "blockage": ["{n}", 10],
        "width": "{w}",
        "space": "{w}"
      }
    },
    "vias": {
      "via1": {
        "gds": "@via1",
        "cut": 0.15,
        "below": "met1",
        "above": "met2",
        "enc_below": [0.055, 0.085],
        "enc_above": [0.055, 0.085]
      },
      "via2": {
        "gds": "@via2",
        "cut": 0.2,
        "below": "met2",
        "above": "met3",
        "enc_below": [0.04, 0.085],
        "enc_above": [0.065, 0.065]
      }
    }
  },
  "_comment_routing": "sd_via: placed on every contact_layer (met1) column over over_layer (diff) of a MOS to measure gap.x_routed, the row gap at which neighbouring S/D contacts can take different wires up to met2 (vias_gen min via is 0.32 x 0.26, r90 puts the 0.26 side across the 0.23 column). tracks: met2 wires running along a row channel. channel_layer: row gaps are poly to poly.",
  "channel_layer": "@poly",
  "sd_via": {
    "pcell": "vias_gen",
    "fixed": {"start_layer": "metal1", "end_layer": "metal2", "w": 0, "l": 0},
    "orient": "r90",
    "contact_layer": "@met1",
    "over_layer": "@diff",
    "for_class": ["nmos", "pmos"]
  },
  "tracks": {"layer": "@met2"},
  "_comment_policy": "Layout choices, not DRC: poly-to-poly gap between matched rows is at least row_gap_poly_min and the channel tracks need, rounded up to row_gap_round (user 2026-11-04; 05_miller_ota had 0.42 at the DP gates and 1.54 in the bias mirror).",
  "layout_policy": {"row_gap_poly_min": 1.0, "row_gap_round": 0.1},
  "_comment_annotation": "Non-mask layer for the slot names export_gds.py writes (235/4 prBoundary.boundary is ignored by DRC and LVS).",
  "annotation_layer": "@prBoundary",
  "_comment_blockage": "Layer for the outer-router blockage box of each routed block (lib/block_router routing.blockages), drawn by export_gds.py for viewing only. 250/0 is in no sky130 layer map, so DRC and LVS ignore it (metN.blockage 6x/10 is checked by the KLayout deck: m1.3ab, m2.3ab, m3.3ab).",
